Fixed: The 'stress second invariant' visualization postprocessor
included part of the pressure in 2d models. Since #6471 it took the
plane-strain consistent deviator (trace/3) of the total stress, which
in 2d lacks the out-of-plane component sigma_zz = p, so the output was
sqrt(tau_II^2 + p^2/3) instead of tau_II. It now computes the invariant
from the deviatoric stress only. Results in 3d are unchanged.
